WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.050
Start with something nobody had to teach you.

2
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:08.510
Anything that can feel prefers pleasure to pain,

3
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.430
and keeps trying to make its life go better.

4
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.070
You did it this morning.

5
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.750
So did everyone you passed on the way.

6
00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.330
People describe their choices differently,

7
00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:23.350
but the drive is the same in all of us: a life that goes well.

8
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.523
The philosophy calls it life's primary mission.

9
00:00:27.423 --> 00:00:30.043
Now think of the best stretch of your life.

10
00:00:30.043 --> 00:00:34.223
Not one good day: a year or two when things were working.

11
00:00:34.223 --> 00:00:36.023
What was true then?

12
00:00:36.023 --> 00:00:38.483
Most people give the same answers.

13
00:00:38.483 --> 00:00:39.923
I was safe.

14
00:00:39.923 --> 00:00:42.283
What I earned was mine to keep.

15
00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:44.183
My time was my own.

16
00:00:44.183 --> 00:00:48.103
And the people around me were there because they chose to be.

17
00:00:48.103 --> 00:00:50.623
It is not only you.

18
00:00:50.623 --> 00:00:55.223
Psychologists who study well-being in dozens of countries keep finding the same

19
00:00:55.223 --> 00:01:00.043
needs: to choose your own course, to be close to people you trust,

20
00:01:00.043 --> 00:01:01.823
and to get good at something.

21
00:01:01.823 --> 00:01:04.245
None of it lasts if you are not safe.

22
00:01:05.145 --> 00:01:06.965
Now the hardest stretch.

23
00:01:06.965 --> 00:01:13.125
Some hardship is nobody's doing: an illness, a loss, plain bad luck.

24
00:01:13.125 --> 00:01:16.945
Set that aside and look at the part that was done to you.

25
00:01:16.945 --> 00:01:18.585
Someone threatened you.

26
00:01:18.585 --> 00:01:22.045
Someone took what was yours, or cheated you out of it.

27
00:01:22.045 --> 00:01:26.045
Someone decided how your days were spent, and you could not leave.

28
00:01:26.045 --> 00:01:28.985
You were probably frustrated enough to swear.

29
00:01:28.985 --> 00:01:32.436
Did that happen because you felt happier, or less happy?

30
00:01:33.336 --> 00:01:37.056
And notice that it cost you three things, not one.

31
00:01:37.056 --> 00:01:40.236
Happiness: you felt that at once.

32
00:01:40.236 --> 00:01:44.276
Harmony: think what it did between you and the person who did it.

33
00:01:44.276 --> 00:01:48.516
The trust was gone, and part of you wanted to get even.

34
00:01:48.516 --> 00:01:51.276
Prosperity: think what you did next.

35
00:01:51.276 --> 00:01:52.556
You locked things.

36
00:01:52.556 --> 00:01:53.776
You hid things.

37
00:01:53.776 --> 00:01:57.456
You stopped planning, because why build what can be taken?

38
00:01:57.456 --> 00:02:03.336
That is what flourishing means: happiness, harmony and prosperity together.

39
00:02:03.336 --> 00:02:06.043
One act of force went through all three.

40
00:02:06.943 --> 00:02:12.243
The philosophy calls this a principle, and it means the word the way physics does.

41
00:02:12.243 --> 00:02:13.743
Nobody made it up.

42
00:02:13.743 --> 00:02:18.343
It describes cause and effect: do this, and that follows,

43
00:02:18.343 --> 00:02:20.136
whether anyone likes it or not.

44
00:02:21.036 --> 00:02:25.356
Gravity works the same whatever you meant to do, and so does this.

45
00:02:25.356 --> 00:02:29.908
The harm arrives whatever the reason was, and however good the cause.

46
00:02:30.808 --> 00:02:31.988
But always?

47
00:02:31.988 --> 00:02:34.428
Surely force sometimes works.

48
00:02:34.428 --> 00:02:37.468
The money was taken, and the clinic got built.

49
00:02:37.468 --> 00:02:39.208
Take that seriously.

50
00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:42.648
A plane in the air has not switched gravity off.

51
00:02:42.648 --> 00:02:47.408
Gravity pulls on it every second, and it pays in fuel the whole way.

52
00:02:47.408 --> 00:02:50.928
When force seems to work, the cost is still there.

53
00:02:50.928 --> 00:02:52.556
It is just harder to see.

54
00:02:53.456 --> 00:02:54.896
Look at what was paid.

55
00:02:54.896 --> 00:03:00.056
The person it was taken from is less happy: you have been that person.

56
00:03:00.056 --> 00:03:03.716
Between them and whoever took it, there is now a grievance.

57
00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:07.356
They organize to win that power and use it the other way,

58
00:03:07.356 --> 00:03:11.976
and the philosophy has a name for what follows: a conflict machine.

59
00:03:11.976 --> 00:03:15.876
And people who are made to give, give the least they can.

60
00:03:15.876 --> 00:03:17.816
The clinic is real.

61
00:03:17.816 --> 00:03:21.736
But time, talent and money built it, not the force.

62
00:03:21.736 --> 00:03:27.056
There are three ways to gather those: share your own, persuade others to join you,

63
00:03:27.056 --> 00:03:28.136
or force them.

64
00:03:28.136 --> 00:03:31.639
Only one of the three puts the principle against you.

65
00:03:32.539 --> 00:03:35.099
So here is the test in one line.

66
00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:36.559
Find the exception.

67
00:03:36.559 --> 00:03:41.619
One time, as an adult, when you were threatened, robbed or made to obey,

68
00:03:41.619 --> 00:03:46.259
and came away happier, closer to the person who did it, and better off.

69
00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.299
Some people have an answer ready.

70
00:03:48.299 --> 00:03:51.099
I was arrested, and it turned my life around.

71
00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:54.419
I got mugged walking home and spent a week in hospital,

72
00:03:54.419 --> 00:03:57.159
and I found out who my real friends were.

73
00:03:57.159 --> 00:03:59.339
But look at what did the good.

74
00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.079
You chose to change.

75
00:04:01.079 --> 00:04:02.539
They chose to visit.

76
00:04:02.539 --> 00:04:06.939
The force only took from you: the years, the week in pain.

77
00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:10.119
The good came in spite of it, not because of it.

78
00:04:10.119 --> 00:04:12.999
Find a time the force itself did the good.

79
00:04:12.999 --> 00:04:14.363
That is your exception.

80
00:04:15.263 --> 00:04:21.383
Coercion, theft and violence always reduce happiness, harmony and prosperity.

81
00:04:21.383 --> 00:04:22.430
Always.

82
00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:28.110
And if that is how the world works, the conclusion is about your own interest.

83
00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:32.910
The surest way to your own good life is to deal with people by persuasion,

84
00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:37.814
in every part of it: at home, at work, and in your community.

85
00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:44.534
Most people agree by now, and add one thing.

86
00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:48.274
Fine, but I do not rob or threaten anyone.

87
00:04:48.274 --> 00:04:49.414
Probably not.

88
00:04:49.414 --> 00:04:52.654
But have you ever asked someone else to do it for you?

89
00:04:52.654 --> 00:04:55.634
That is next: Human Agency.

90
00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:59.927
The whole series, in order, is at humanrespect.app.
